# List of expectations for tests that do not match their expected images,
# one per line.
# There are seven space-separated columns per line
# Each column (except column 0) can contain a comma-separated list of values.
#
# Column 0: test file name
# Column 1: platform: *, win, mac, mac_arm, mac_x86, linux
# Column 2: v8 support: *, nov8, v8
# Column 3: xfa support: *, noxfa, xfa
# Column 4: rendering support: *, agg, gdi, gdi_agg, gdi_skia, skia
# Column 5: font engine: *, freetype, fontations
# Column 6: action, one of:
#   diff  - the output differs in a way that no tolerance can bridge, so
#           the test still runs but never fails, however far off it lands
#   blank - skip the image comparison entirely
#   fuzzy - compare with a tolerance, either the defaults or the explicit
#           fuzzy=<delta>,<mse>,<win_mse> (e.g. fuzzy=3,0.05,15.0)
#   skip  - the test is expected to crash, so do not run it at all
#
# Apart from "skip", every action excuses mismatching output and nothing
# else. A crash, an ASan report, a CHECK failure or a timeout is reported
# as a failure no matter what is listed here, even when the test managed
# to write output that matches.
#
# All columns on a line must match, but filenames may be repeated on subsequent
# lines to suppress more cases.  Within each column, any one of the
# comma-separated values must match in order for the column to "match".
# The filenames and keywords are case-sensitive.
# One exception is column 1, where "mac" is a shorthand that matches either
# "mac_arm" or "mac_x86". Similarly, "gdi" in column 4 is a shorthand that
# matches either "gdi_agg" or "gdi_skia".
#
# Try to keep the file alphabetized within each category of test.

